    "note": "Today against a month ago. Monday lifted the whole curve by 6–8bp: the two-year to 4.92%, the ten-year to 5.24% and the thirty-year to 5.56%, the ten-year's highest close since 2007 and the long bond's highest in more than two decades. Every maturity from three years out now yields above 5%; the two-year is 8bp short. Reported closes on Monday were 4.93% on the two-year, 5.236% on the ten and about 5.57% on the thirty; the source table prints 4.92%, 5.24% and 5.56%, which is what the curve above draws. No coupon supply this week; the ten-year and thirty-year auctions land on 7 and 8 October.",
